From: xiaoxiaoafeifei <xiaoxiaoafeifei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 7 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] security(io): fix stack-buffer-underflow in IOFile::getLine (CVE-2026-75421)

When a line read from an input file, session file, cookie file, or config
begins with a NUL byte, strlen(buf.data()) returns 0 and buf[len - 1]
reads buf[-1]. Guard with len > 0 before indexing.

Upstream PR: https://github.com/aria2/aria2/pull/2376
Upstream Issue: https://github.com/aria2/aria2/issues/2375
CVE: CVE-2026-75421
---
 src/IOFile.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/IOFile.cc b/src/IOFile.cc
--- a/src/IOFile.cc
+++ b/src/IOFile.cc
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ std::string IOFile::getLine()
   while (gets(buf.data(), buf.size())) {
     size_t len = strlen(buf.data());
     bool lineBreak = false;
-    if (buf[len - 1] == '\n') {
+    if (len > 0 && buf[len - 1] == '\n') {
       --len;
       lineBreak = true;
     }
-- 
